SUMMARY
======================================================================================================================
  f_ret (CFG416)          = retained baryon fraction, M_b/(f_b M_ta) in (0, 0.90]  -> f_ret = 0.10 = 10% of the catchment's baryons
  N = R_cosmic/f_ret      = cold mass / system baryons = 53.64 at f_ret = 0.10 (DERIVED, not a second f_ret)
  f_s (A43's 'f_ret')     = cold mass / SYSTEM cosmic share = 1.00 (system model), 10.00 (A44), 2.19 (A43) -- ceiling 1 is the system denominator
  f_c = f_s f_ret^b       = cold mass / CATCHMENT cosmic share = 1.000 at A44's model, 0.219 at A43's EOS reading (ceiling 1)
  factor 10               = 1/f_ret (baryon reservoir), NOT a density; 1+delta_cold(r_e) = 133, 1+delta_cold(0.1 Mpc) = 5499
  53.64 M_b available?    = 44.1 M_b at 1e11 (82% of it), 37.9 at the top bin; N_req = 15.9
  decisive number         = N_avail/N_req = 2.38 > 1  -> not capped; tension does not return on the primary range
  dchi2 at the available budget = -0.4 vs +1.1 at 53.64 (both <= 4)

